<p><img loading="lazy" decoding="async" class="aligncenter wp-image-88005 size-full" src="https://www.toysnbricks.com/wp-content/uploads/2024/02/18-LEGO-Icons-10330-McLaren-MP4-4-Ayrton-Senna-March-2024-Release-Date.jpg" alt="" width="980" height="520" srcset="https://www.toysnbricks.com/wp-content/uploads/2024/02/18-LEGO-Icons-10330-McLaren-MP4-4-Ayrton-Senna-March-2024-Release-Date.jpg 980w, https://www.toysnbricks.com/wp-content/uploads/2024/02/18-LEGO-Icons-10330-McLaren-MP4-4-Ayrton-Senna-March-2024-Release-Date-300x159.jpg 300w, https://www.toysnbricks.com/wp-content/uploads/2024/02/18-LEGO-Icons-10330-McLaren-MP4-4-Ayrton-Senna-March-2024-Release-Date-768x408.jpg 768w" sizes="auto, (max-width: 980px) 100vw, 980px" /></p>
<p><span style="font-weight: 400;">If you are 10 bucks short of getting the Ferrari F2004 set, you can consider the McLaren MP4/4 &amp; Ayrton Senna model. It still has an iconic minifigure–Ayrton Senna, who won 3 World Drivers’ Championships. 41 race wins is also an impressive feat considering his age.</span></p>
<p><span style="font-weight: 400;">The McLaren MP4/4 &amp; Ayrton Senna set has 693 pieces. While it has fewer pieces than the Ferrari, you still get authentic details like the rod suspension, an adjustable rear wing, and a working steering. I don’t suppose you will be taking it for a “ride” often. But if you choose to keep it for display, like </span><a href="https://www.toysnbricks.com/11-upcoming-lego-speed-champions-march-2027-sets-revealed-release-dates-us-canada-prices-set-images/"><span style="font-weight: 400;">LEGO Speed Champions</span></a><span style="font-weight: 400;">, you’ll find the information plaque particularly useful, with some eye-catching details.</span></p>
<p><span style="font-weight: 400;">For more details, you have the turbocharged V6 engine, gearshift, mirrors, and slick tyres. It’s a 1988 racer. Hence, you can expect the vintage feel when you assemble and display it.</span></p>
